are called conditionally independent given C if probability of A intersection B given

207
00:21:18,270 --> 00:21:23,520
C equals to probability of A given C into probability of B given C. This condition

208
00:21:23,520 --> 00:21:27,060
is very similar in form to the previous condition for independence of events.

209
00:21:27,060 --> 00:21:35,100
Equivalently the events A and B are conditionally independent given C if probability of A given B

210
00:21:35,100 --> 00:21:40,050
intersection C is equal to probability of A given C. This latter condition is quite

211
00:21:40,050 --> 00:21:49,140
informative. What it says is that the probability of A calculated after knowing the occurrence of

212
00:21:49,140 --> 00:21:57,150
event C is same as the probability of A calculated after having knowledge of occurrence of both

213
00:21:57,150 --> 00:22:04,800
events B and C thus observing the occurrence or non-occurrence of B does not provide any extra

214
00:22:04,800 --> 00:22:11,880
information. And thus we can conclude that the events A and B are conditions independent given C.

215
00:22:11,880 --> 00:22:17,340
Let us consider an example assume that admission into the M.Tech program at IIT

216
00:22:17,340 --> 00:22:22,530
Madras in IIT Bombay is based solely on candidates GATE score. Then probability

217
00:22:22,530 --> 00:22:28,470
of admission into IIT Madras given knowledge of the candidate’s admission status in IIT

218
00:22:28,470 --> 00:22:33,240
Bombay as well as the candidate’s GATE score is equivalent to the probability calculated

219
00:22:33,240 --> 00:22:39,300
simply knowing the candidate’s GATE score. Thus knowing the status of the candidates

220
00:22:39,300 --> 00:22:46,350
admission into IIT Bombay does not provide any extra information. Hence since the condition is

221
00:22:46,350 --> 00:22:51,810
satisfied we can say that admission into the program at IIT Madras and admission into the

222
00:22:51,810 --> 00:22:56,430
program at IIT Bombay are independent events given knowledge of the candidates GATE score.
